    doc+='<section id="unknown"><h2>The failed full run remains a separate recorded experiment</h2><p>The original remaining-86 producer completed and saved every exact-request heap estimate. During its subsequent common-workspace serialization it exceeded the unchanged 512 MiB process ceiling after saving 37 of the 94 encodings. Its status remains <code>unknown_full_capacity_memory_budget</code>; the missing 57 encodings were unresolved in that experiment. No native query or proof search ran.</p><p>A separate independent replay checked every instruction event, profile, complete canonical heap and record-width sum for all 86 new estimates, retained the eight earlier audited estimates, and reconstructed precisely the 37 saved encoded inputs. It did not retroactively complete the failed run. The scoped partial audit preserves all 57 missing encodings explicitly.</p><p>The old serializer accumulated a full integer vector and unpacked it as a large argument list. The repair is a new source version: it emits the identical little-endian format in bounded chunks directly to compressed output. The separate auditor uses a typed array and reconstructs each full input independently. Neither repair changes the mathematical problem, requests, alphabet, parser/checker instructions, palette, band capacities or encoding semantics.</p></section>'
