    doc+='<section id="catalog"><h2>Complete finite request accounting</h2><p>The complete structurally retained union contains 94 local definitions. One whole request is byte-identical to an earlier fully audited zero-left interface admission; its historical checking cost is preserved and it may receive exact-request reuse credit in a later admission registry. The other 93 requests require fresh native admission. The complete grammar and every alternative remain in the <a href="commutativity_feasibility.html#grammar">frozen feasibility report</a>.</p><details><summary>All 94 estimates, in ascending exact definition-name order</summary>'+table(['Index','Local primitive commands','Whole request bytes','Tree instructions','Exact heap cells','Fits original heap','Native status at this gate'],rows)+'</details><p>The row index is a catalog index, not a proof line or chosen derivation. Exact definition names, request hashes, all primitive commands and initial frames are available in the downloadable request inventory, metric catalog and complete evidence archives. This full accounting was prepared without selecting a target proof.</p></section>'
